{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Choose for us men.</b> Who were born in the second Adar, and they need not fear sorceries, for it has no mazal (astral sign), and the children of Amalek are sorcerers and have power through the twelve mazalot, and when it has no mazal, no sorcery succeeds. Another interpretation: <b>Choose for us men</b> — so that the number of our forces and theirs be equal." "<b>I will stand on the top of the hill.</b> So that the men of the army see me, to give their hearts resolve to go strong into battle, as it is said, 'and Joshua did not withdraw his hand that he stretched out with the javelin until he had destroyed,' etc., for such is the way of men of battle: one of their champions stands in a high place and holds a banner in his hand, because all the men who go out with him to battle keep their eyes fixed on the banner. As long as it stands in its place, they take heart and strengthen themselves for battle; and when the banner drops low, they think their commander has fallen and flee. So too here: 'and the staff of Elohim in my hand' — as a sign and symbol in place of a banner."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:22.624743419Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}